and reading.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I am about to sit my GCSEs in : physics, chemistry, biology, maths, English literature, English language, french, history, geography and fine art', 'special_interests' => 'I take part in a STEM potential course once every other month as part of the open schools partenership, this is held in the Scitech building at Oundle private school.  I qualified as a bellboat helm for guiding and scouting with the BCU course. I assisted in the setting up of an anti-bullying peer mentor scheme at my school which also lead to us applying for, and being accepted to receive a grant from the queens commonwealth trust to renovate a room which we now use to help people  struggling with bullying . In March if 2019 we were interviewed by the QCT for their website and Instagram page', 'special_skills' => 'I have supervised Brownies in bouldering at Peterborough climbing wall and completed a course that allows me to boulder without supervision, but due to the closure of the climbing wall I did the course at I will have to retake it. I have also belayed on multiple occasions when climbing, but am not qualified. I have been a young leader at Brownies and Rainbows, as well as helping with the Guide unit for multiple years.', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I do not play any instruments other than playing the guitar, but not to any level at which I could contribute.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'My Grandfather is a Rotarian heavily involved in youth exchange so I have always seen photos of camps from him, so I decided it was something I would like to take the opportunity and do in the summer after my GCSEs . I am interested in the Valentina camp because of its activities which link to my interests as well as being in a part of the world I have never visited before. I am also interested in the gliding camp in Lithuania as I love aviation and hope to become a pilot one day.', 'personal_remarks' => 'I am a very keen learner and l like my schoolwork, I really enjoy learning new things about culture and new activities and I hope this is something I will be able to take with me on the camp and pass on to others, and see what they can teach me and I look forward to taking away experiences and new ideas from the people I meet.', 'place_of_birth' => 'Peterborough, Cambridgeshire, England', 'em_name' => 'Conny Yarwood ', 'em_relationship' => 'Grandmother', 'em_htel' => '+44 1733 394669', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7712 704163', 'em_email' => 'Applemany@icloud.com', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3746.jpeg', 'date_of_app' => '2019-09-14 20:53:00'],
