tre for children with special needs. My interests also include Karate. I now have a brown-black belt and I  attained a bronze life-saving swimming certificate.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I am currently studying at Advanced Level (A-level) and chose to study biology, maths and welsh baccalaureate. This is because I would like to study Biomedical Science at university and feel very passionate about it. I completed my General Certificate for Secondary Education in which I took the subjects Sociology, Information Communication & Technology (ICT) and French.', 'special_interests' => 'I participated in the Rotary Youth Leadership Award (RYLA) course back in July at Storey Arms and enjoyed every aspect of it.  I also enrolled myself onto the ilead programme which is a leadership programme involving presenting and learning skills on how to become a good leader for a group. Before applying for the RYLA course, I completed my Duke of Edinburgh Award which involved me using a map and navigating as well as working in a team to overcome challenges such as issues between any team members.', 'special_skills' => 'I speak several languages and read Arabic. I swim and practice karate. I use my computer skills for many tasks, for example creating databases and desktop publishing - I recently created posters to advertise a local festival.', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I can tell many fascinating stories and events that have occurred which would be enjoyable to listen to and am also good at telling jokes which would make it easier for people to get comfortable.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'To gain and understand other cultures through meeting new people, I would also like to become more independent after having completed this course which is why I would think this would be a great opportunity for me', 'personal_remarks' => 'After having done DofE and going through many challenges and achievements, it made me want to take on another challenge which is why I applied on to the RYLA course. Throughout that week, I made many friends and became close to a lot of people who were complete strangers before. This is why after experiencing all of that, I was interested in going an extra level forward in Rotary and apply for this wonderful opportunity to take part in a Rotary Youth Camp Exchange.', 'place_of_birth' => 'Newport, Wales, UK', 'em_name' => 'Ambreen Khan', 'em_relationship' => 'Aunt', 'em_htel' => '+44 1633 893987', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7586 901563', 'em_email' => 'khanambreens@yahoo.co.uk', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3762.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-09-21 18:12:00'],
            ['idapplication' => '868', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => true, 'dob' => '1997-09-10', 'gender' => true, 'email_address' => 'wisabelle97@gmail.com', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'A Rotarian recommended it', 'firstname' => 'Isabelle', 'surname' => 'Winter', 'address' => '16 Grayson Way', 'city' => 'Cwmbran', 'county' => 'Torfaen', 'postcode' => 'NP44 3GD', 'contact_no' => '', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7984 598924', 'parent_1' => 'Melanie Winter', 'parent_2' => 'Darren Winter', 'application_no' => '3763', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => 'Isabelle', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1150', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Accepted', 'application_status_note' => 'Paid Admin Fee', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'winter.melano@gmail.com', 'parent2_email' => 'wnerrad68@yahoo.co.uk', 'parent1_tel' => '', 'parent2_tel' => '', 'parent1_mobile' => '07958140789', 'parent2_mobile' => '07706706582', 'parent1_btel' => '', 'parent2_btel' => '', 'parent1_occupation' => 'Paralegal officer', 'parent2_occupation' => 'Therapeutic Social Worker', 'religion' => 'N/A', 'diet_restriction' => 'None', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => true, 'drink_why' => 'I am allowed to drink alcohol and do at times socially, however I do not drink excessively or regularly. ', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => false, 'treated_condition' => true, 'prescribed_meds' => false, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => 'I have suffered with anxiety for the past few years, however I have had counselling and this has improved dramatically. ', 'rotary_club_id' => '19665', 'free_activities' => 'Music, art and languages are my passions as well as spending time with friends and family. My free time is much more limited due to being a student, however finding the time to participate in activities that help me to relax really helps with my progression and development in my University course. Keeping active is also an important factor in my daily routine, such as walking up mountains and going for runs. This helps clear my mind and improve my overall fitness, all of which can prepare me to face any challenges that are thrown my way. ', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I am a student at University of Leicester studying French and Spanish. I have achieved 12 GCSE\'s receiving grades between A*-B, along with 4 A levels: B\'s in Spanish, French and English, and an A in Welsh Baccalaureate. I also achieved an A in AS level Art. I undertook my statutory education through the medium of the Welsh language. Although this provided challenges particularly when translating from French to Welsh, for example, it has improved my language skills and it has also taught me the importance of languages to enhance our cultural understanding of the world. ', 'special_interests' => 'I am a very creative person, so my special interests include most activities in this field. I enjoy facing new challenges, while constantly testing my boundaries. As an example, I have promoted the Rotary Club through presentations in many events, despite having a fear of public speaking. As a result, my confidence has improved significantly and I no longer suffer with this. Furthermore, I have participated in the Rotary Youth Leadership Programme which tested not only my physical ability, but my ability to interact with a new group of people.  Additionally, I have achieved my Grade 7 in the piano and the harp. ', 'special_skills' => 'I pride myself on my ability to speak 4 languages and it would be very interesting to meet other fluent speakers of any of these languages to converse with. Aside from playing musical instruments, I love art and I would class painting/drawing as a special skill of mine. Singing, for me, is a way of relaxing and a passion that I have pursued from a young age. Through my participation in the University choir, it is possible for me to have some time away from my studies, and be immersed in music. This makes it not only a special skill, but an essential skill to de-stress. ', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'As I enjoy playing the harp, the piano and singing, this could definitely contribute to entertainment. I enjoy sharing my passions with others and I would be very much willing to contribute to any social activities in order to make the most of my time in the camp. ', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I am an independent individual who thrives on new experiences, meeting new people and travelling as much as I can. My experience within Rotary has provided me with only a small insight into what the club truly represents and I am eager to explore this further. I am excited to meet potentially like-minded people with similar passions and a keen interest in discovering more about the world. ', 'personal_remarks' => 'I am a focused and hard-working individual with a passion for life and a genuine interest in what the world has to offer. It is my ambition to travel to as many countries as possible, purely to witness the array of cultures and languages that surround us. Each individual, despite their nationality, ethnicity or religion, has a different story to share. It is in this way that I have an interest to improve my cultural knowledge through meeting new people and to learn about their heritage, and to hopefully gain a deeper understanding of the world that we live in.  ', 'place_of_birth' => 'Newport, Gwent', 'em_name' => 'Sharon Winter ', 'em_relationship' => 'Step-mother ', 'em_htel' => '', 'em_mobile' => '07590254136', 'em_email' => 'sharon@cf-cs.co.uk', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3763.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-09-21 19:19:00'],
