8 in both piano and singing so practise both on a regular basis. Walking is something I enjoy as I consider myself an extrovert and like to appreciate my surroundings. I am passionate about the environment and hope to become an engineer due to my interest in STEM and my intentions of creating/developing sustainable alternatives. I also attend gym classes, do hockey, swimming, rock climbing and bowling in order to keep active in the week.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I currently attend the King\'s School Peterborough - I obtained placement there through academic ability. I take pride in my schoolwork and am predicted 7-9s in my GCSE examinations in the upcoming year. Regarding my GCSE options, I opted to take French, Product Design and Geography, as I believe they would be most helpful in helping me reach my goal to become a respected engineer.', 'special_interests' => 'As I mentioned above, I play the piano and sing and have ABRSM certification in both (for grade 7). For over a year, I was a member of the Air Training Corps and, in this time, took part in a regional competition where we competed with team exercises, First Aid, drill and a music performance. During my time as an air cadet, I also went on a bronze radio communications and received certificates in First aid and shooting.In October half term, I attended a \'Routes Into STEM\' course and obtained a Bronze industrial Cadet Award. This year I hope to get a place on the Bronze DofE programme offered at my school. ', 'special_skills' => 'First aid: I have a St John\'s Ambulance first aid qualification as I took part in a 12-hour course and passed assessment.
Music: ABRSM grade 7 in Piano and Voice, previous member of the Peterborough Youth choir, current member of my church choir.
Sport: Vice-captain of The King\'s School Hockey team in Y7; Captain of the King\'s School KS3 Dodgeball team (in Y9). In rock climbing, am Competent in Belaying and tying appropriate knots (passed introductory lesson assessment)
General: Strong teamwork, communication and leadership skills developed through time in Cadets.
', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'Yes, I have musical ability, as mentioned above.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'The main reason for my participation in the programme is to take the opportunity to meet new people and learn more about other cultures and developing my personal confidence through this. I am particularly interested in camps related to learning about the environment as it is very important to me.', 'personal_remarks' => '', 'place_of_birth' => 'Cagayan De Oro, Misamis Oriental, Philippines', 'em_name' => 'Mary Brick', 'em_relationship' => 'Family Friend', 'em_htel' => '+44 1733 267877', 'em_mobile' => '', 'em_email' => '', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3779.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-09-25 20:01:00'],
            ['idapplication' => '885', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => true, 'dob' => '2003-05-11', 'gender' => true, 'email_address' => 'flomo.ophelia@yahoo.com', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'Presentation at School/College/University', 'firstname' => 'Ophelia', 'surname' => 'Flomo', 'address' => '20 Townsend Close', 'city' => 'Peterborough', 'county' => 'Cambridge', 'postcode' => 'PE1 2SQ', 'contact_no' => '+44 1733 851779', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7910 704143', 'parent_1' => 'Troh leontine sonia flomo', 'parent_2' => 'fankan siloman marcel flomo', 'application_no' => '3780', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => 'Ophelia', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1070', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Accepted', 'application_status_note' => 'Paid Admin Fee', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'troh.flomo@yahoo.co.uk', 'parent2_email' => 'molof21@gmail.com', 'parent1_tel' => '', 'parent2_tel' => '', 'parent1_mobile' => '+44 7981 202461', 'parent2_mobile' => '', 'parent1_btel' => '', 'parent2_btel' => '', 'parent1_occupation' => 'civil servant', 'parent2_occupation' => '', 'religion' => 'Christian', 'diet_restriction' => 'none', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => false, 'drink_why' => '', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => false, 'treated_condition' => true, 'prescribed_meds' => false, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => 'My asthma was treated ', 'rotary_club_id' => '19144', 'free_activities' => 'I enjoy reading in my spare time, I also enjoy cooking and following new recipes. In addition I like eating out and trying new foods. Currently, I am volunteering at a charity shop once a week. ', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I attend the Kings school Peterborough and I am in sixthform studying studying French, Biology and Chemistry at A levels. I am currently a student commissioner. In year six I achieved the position of head girl.  Throughout secondary school, I achieved the title of learning leader in the subjects Religious studies, French and Food technology. I was a \'hero\' as part of a mentoring programme which involved children lower down in the school. I also attainted GCSE\'s grades (A*-B). ', 'special_interests' => 'In year six, I had a poem published and had another published a year later at the start of primary school. I graduated from NCS last summer in which I was away for 3 weeks in total. During that time I learned life skills and experienced the university lifestyle and I also volunteered for one week at an old people\'s home, I feel like we had a big impact on them as we helped clear up and decorate their gardens. We also organised coffee mornings and afternoon games activities in which they could take part in. ', 'special_skills' => 'I\'d say I have a skill for writing as I\'ve been quite passionate about it for a long time and I\'ve achieved things to do with writing too. I\'d say one of my skills is cooking as my dad was a chef and taught me a lot of cuisine skills when I was younger.', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I can\'t think of anything in particular however I could possibly write and read a poem?', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I\'d like to develop my language and social skills, I\'d also like to meet new people from different cultures and backgrounds as in the future I\'d love a job where I could do that. I also want to travel and experience new things  and activities. Personally, this seems like a rare opportunity which I am very lucky to have come across so I definitely wouldn\'t want to miss out. ', 'personal_remarks' => '', 'place_of_birth' => 'London, England', 'em_name' => 'Rochelle', 'em_relationship' => 'family friend', 'em_htel' => '', 'em_mobile' => '', 'em_email' => '', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3780.jpeg', 'date_of_app' => '2019-09-25 20:44:00'],
