 as the local rugby club, which I play at twice a week. I also enjoy keeping fit in general, going to the gym quite regularly or playing football with friends. Away from sport, I love reading books and enjoy watching films and going to the cinema with friends and family. ', 'attainment_vocation' => 'GCSE Maths, English Literature, English Language, French, History, RE, Geography, Science
BTEC PE, ICT', 'special_interests' => 'Level 2 rugby referee
Northants DPP rugby programme
Duke of Edinburgh Bronze award', 'special_skills' => 'I have good interpersonal skills, and can hold conversation with most people. I would consider myself reliable, and appreciate the importance of being presentable and responsible. I also think I have a good sense of humour, and enjoy other people\'s company. In general I think I\'m quite confident, whether that is doing something as a group or by myself- I try to always be involved. ', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I can play guitar ', 'reason_for_camp' => 'One of the main reasons is that I\'m keen to experience sport abroad, in particular rugby in a different country with people who are like me. I love travelling to different countries and experiencing new culture, through food, the physical aspects of the country, and by the people that I might meet during my time there. I believe that through sport, people break down barriers between each other, and come together to enjoy something that they share a common love of, and so through a camp, I would love to do this, combining my interest in culture with my love of sport.   ', 'personal_remarks' => '', 'place_of_birth' => 'Huntingdon, UK', 'em_name' => 'Andrea Racey', 'em_relationship' => 'family friend', 'em_htel' => '', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7808 165933', 'em_email' => 'a.racey5@gmail.com', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3794.jpeg', 'date_of_app' => '2019-10-02 19:00:00'],
