            ['idapplication' => '910', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => false, 'dob' => '2003-04-01', 'gender' => true, 'email_address' => 'mbolton334@gmail.com', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'Other', 'firstname' => 'Molly', 'surname' => 'Bolton', 'address' => '1 New England Cottages, Wennington,', 'city' => 'Huntingdon', 'county' => 'Cambridgeshire', 'postcode' => 'PE28 2LP', 'contact_no' => '+44 7734 871066', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7791 633056', 'parent_1' => 'Becky Bolton', 'parent_2' => 'Nick Bolton ', 'application_no' => '3809', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => 'Molly', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1070', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Placed', 'application_status_note' => 'Paid Admin Fee (rolled-over), Early Bird TURE05 Turkey', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'becky@motiv8.co.uk', 'parent2_email' => 'Nick@electriccorby.co.uk', 'parent1_tel' => '', 'parent2_tel' => '', 'parent1_mobile' => '+44 7791 633056', 'parent2_mobile' => '+44 7734 871066', 'parent1_btel' => '', 'parent2_btel' => '+44 1536 560222', 'parent1_occupation' => 'Midwife', 'parent2_occupation' => '', 'religion' => 'Christian (Anglican)', 'diet_restriction' => 'None', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => false, 'drink_why' => '', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => false, 'treated_condition' => null, 'prescribed_meds' => false, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => 'March 2019 broke tibia and fibula.  In hospital for 5 days and now have a permanent rod in my left leg.  Was having check ups at Peterborough Hospital regularly until October 23rd. ', 'rotary_club_id' => '19146', 'free_activities' => 'In my spare time, I play for a netball team called Rockets where I take part in training and matches each week. I also row at the weekends for Oundleâ€™s Rowing club. As well as these, I go to fitness classes on a weekly basis with my mum. Recently I have just started volunteering at my local church where I clean the whole church every week. As I am taking Biology for one of my A levels,  I am learning more about the subject outside of school with a tutor.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I currently go to The King\'s (The Cathedral) school sixth form, where  I am studying 3 A levels, Biology, Psychology and Physical Education. I hope to go to university once achieving my target grades for those A levels,  but I am unsure at the moment which subject I will study at  university.', 'special_interests' => 'I like to go places and do activities with my family and friends and spend my time with them. Also enjoy baking and cooking  meals for my family particularly when they\'re  busy at work.  I like exploring new places and learning about different cultures and I went to Montenegro on a 10 day hiking trip in an extreme climate with my school, where we hiked up challenging mountains with 20kg rucksacks, camps in the wild for 5 days and had no phones on the trip. I think this was an accomplishment as I broke my leg very badly and had to train extremely hard afterwards to be allowed to go on the trip.', 'special_skills' => 'Cooking!
Very good at explaining exercises.
Photography', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I like to play board games', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I am keen to go to another country and meet new people to learn about the country and culture. I am a very sociable person and get on well with people, so feel I can contribute fully to interacting with fellow participants on the programme.
My sister has done two Youth Camps which she thoroughly enjoyed and following on from these programmes it gave her the confidence to travel and experience new challenges and she has gone on to travel independently since. I am hoping that this will give me the same confidence,  in a safe and enjoyable environment.', 'personal_remarks' => 'Looking forward to meeting everyone and thank you for the opportunity.', 'place_of_birth' => 'Huntingdon, Cambridgeshire, England ', 'em_name' => 'Helen Leve', 'em_relationship' => 'Aunt', 'em_htel' => '+44 1543 473116', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7469 879359', 'em_email' => 'helen.discovery@yahoo.co.uk', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3809.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-10-13 15:35:00'],
            ['idapplication' => '911', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => false, 'dob' => '2001-09-10', 'gender' => true, 'email_address' => 'jessica.wood2001@outlook.com', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'A Rotarian recommended it', 'firstname' => 'Jessica', 'surname' => 'Wood', 'address' => '19 Lansdowne Road', 'city' => 'Newport', 'county' => 'Gwent', 'postcode' => 'NP20 3FZ', 'contact_no' => '', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7576 894363', 'parent_1' => 'Victoria Williams', 'parent_2' => '', 'application_no' => '3810', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => 'Jess', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1150', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Placed', 'application_status_note' => 'TAI02 Taiwan - Explore Taiwan cycling camp 2020', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'jessica.wood2001@outlook.com', 'parent2_email' => '', 'parent1_tel' => '+44 1633 252694', 'parent2_tel' => '', 'parent1_mobile' => '+44 7864 316251', 'parent2_mobile' => '', 'parent1_btel' => '', 'parent2_btel' => '', 'parent1_occupation' => 'Chemist', 'parent2_occupation' => '', 'religion' => 'Christian', 'diet_restriction' => 'Lactose Intolerant', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => false, 'drink_why' => '', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => false, 'treated_condition' => false, 'prescribed_meds' => false, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => '', 'rotary_club_id' => '19665', 'free_activities' => 'In my free time, I love to play rugby for my college, I also love gardening, aspects such as sowing, growing and yielding make it a very enjoyable and relaxing hobby.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'At GCSE, I got: Mathematics C, Numeracy C, English Language C, English Literature B, Geography B, Welsh C, Welsh Baccalaureate B, Physics C, Chemistry C, and Biology C. This year I completed a course known as CVQO which awarded me with a few more GCSEs. I currently study Public Services at level 3 and am hoping to study Law and Criminology at University next year.', 'special_interests' => 'I\'m really interested in Crime and Law, it\'s what I\'m hoping to study at university. I really love understanding the reason why people commit a crime and then finding out their punishment decided at court. I am also very passionate about the environment and try to be as self-sufficient and sustainable as possible. ', 'special_skills' => 'I love taking care of and looking after my plants in my garden, I love to see them grow and develop into fresh produce.', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I used to play the piano when I was in high school, but I\'m not very good anymore.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'It just looks very interesting and educational, I believe that this opportunity would open me up to many new experiences, traditions, food, languages, and cultures.', 'personal_remarks' => '', 'place_of_birth' => 'Plymouth', 'em_name' => 'Jennifer Martin', 'em_relationship' => 'Aunt', 'em_htel' => '', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7943 311899', 'em_email' => '', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3810.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-10-14 14:43:00'],
