 for 3 years at my local dance studio. In these lessons I demonstrate leadership by running warm ups , classes and choreographing routines. For music, I participate in 2 orchestras a week, as well as my own young string quartet where we rehearse weekly for charity concerts and volunteer work in primary schools, but we also have a successful business in which I deal with all of the professional communications. ', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I just completed my GCSES where I all got all A/A*s. I am extremely proud of this and I hope to finish my A-level with good grades to be able to go to university and study sciences (biochemistry or biological sciences related)
', 'special_interests' => 'As mentioned earlier I am interested in the performing arts. One of my biggest achievements is successfully getting into the National Children\'s Orchestra at a young age. I also have played alongside amateur and professional orchestras , such as the London Philharmonic Orchestra (where I was chosen from many young students in the Leicestershire Schools Music Service). I also am extremely proud with the joint achievements of the quartet- where we have booked gigs at restaurants and private birthday parties. ', 'special_skills' => 'I believe I have good social skills, especially with children as I work with young children on a regular basis. As well as good coaching skills, I have also learnt from this position how to deal with adults. I have also worked with children abroad - on my German Exchange where I helped teach English in our partner school. I also taught basic English sayings, nursery rhymes and used my musical skills when I organised a trip to Japan. Over the two weeks, I went to three different schools from a nursery school to the local high school, and taught them English. We also played many English traditional card and board games.', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I play the viola up to a grade 8 standard.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I had an assembly at my school where the programme was introduced, and I thought it was a wonderful idea. I am excited to immerse myself into new cultures. ', 'personal_remarks' => 'As said earlier, I am excited and ready to meet new people and make some new friends, which I hope will last a lifetime. ', 'place_of_birth' => 'north carolina', 'em_name' => 'Justin Williams', 'em_relationship' => 'Family Friend', 'em_htel' => '', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7764 685091', 'em_email' => '', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => null, 'date_of_app' => '2019-10-30 18:03:00'],
            ['idapplication' => '929', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => false, 'dob' => '1999-07-19', 'gender' => false, 'email_address' => 'Abzjodi@outlook.com', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'Search engine', 'firstname' => 'Abbas Aziz', 'surname' => 'Jodiyawalla', 'address' => '12 Mentmore Close', 'city' => 'London', 'county' => 'United Kingdom', 'postcode' => 'HA3 0EA', 'contact_no' => '+44 20 8537 8615', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7504 053841', 'parent_1' => 'Samira Jodiyawalla', 'parent_2' => 'Aziz Jodiyawalla', 'application_no' => '3829', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => 'Abbas', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1130', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Accepted', 'application_status_note' => 'Paid Admin Fee', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'samira@jodiyawalla.co.uk', 'parent2_email' => 'aziz@jodiyawalla.co.uk', 'parent1_tel' => '+44 20 8537 6815', 'parent2_tel' => '+44 20 8537 8615', 'parent1_mobile' => '+44 7949 372231', 'parent2_mobile' => '+44 7525 729993', 'parent1_btel' => '', 'parent2_btel' => '', 'parent1_occupation' => 'Accountant', 'parent2_occupation' => 'Director', 'religion' => 'Muslim', 'diet_restriction' => 'No pork, no alcohol', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => false, 'drink_why' => '', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => false, 'treated_condition' => false, 'prescribed_meds' => false, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => '', 'rotary_club_id' => '19536', 'free_activities' => 'I enjoy mountaineering (hiking and rock-climbing), cycling, running, badminton and fitness. My hobbies include photography, origami and the Rubik cube, and I enjoy finding new music. I spend a lot of time researching about current affairs, socio-economics and politics.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I am studying Economics at university and I am currently completing a 9 month internship in Taiwan in the middle of my education. Recently in university, my team won a competition to produce a video explaining an economic concept. We also gained the highest mark programming a Sudoku Solver. I have completed the Duke of Edinburgh award in school. ', 'special_interests' => 'My passion is mountaineering, and I actively seek out new challenges. I climbed Mount Kilimanjaro in the summer, and have previously completed numerous hiking challenges. I also love cycling and often do cycling challenges. I am currently training to participate in the Spartan challenge and trail running. I love geography - I know the capital city of every country in the world!', 'special_skills' => 'I consider myself to be an amateur photographer and I am always trying to improve my skill in photography. I have a lot of experience in navigation and regularly lead groups. I am also an experienced cyclist and hiker. I am practicing to be a "speed cuber" and learning advanced Rubik Cube techniques. ', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I love talking to people, sharing past experiences and learning about others, and can also play the flute. ', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I think it is exceptionally important to travel around the world and experience multiculturalism, because it breaks down the barriers to social cohesion that are increasingly present in our societies. Becoming friends with people from other countries is a privilege because you always gain new perspectives about the world - and you also have friends from around the world!', 'personal_remarks' => 'I look forward to developing meaningful and life-long friendships on a Rotary exchange camp. ', 'place_of_birth' => 'London, UK', 'em_name' => 'Huzefa Karimjee', 'em_relationship' => 'Family Friend', 'em_htel' => '', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7931 866277', 'em_email' => 'huzefa786@hotmail.co.uk', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3829.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-11-01 03:31:00'],
