or the past 3 months, I have been volunteering as an assistant coach for the Performance Development squad in my club (ages 8-10), which has been very enjoyable. I have played the piano for 9 years and recently took my ARSM performance diploma. I also play the trombone (6 years) and I took my Grade 8 last year. I participate in lots of music ensembles in my school and have been on many musical residential camps including the National Children\'s Orchestra Main orchestra.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I attend South Hampstead High School and I am a joint music and academic scholar. Last year, I won the Junior Category of the Leah Kiverstein Singing Competition at school and this year received an Academic Achievement Award with the Street Cup for Science. I achieved a Silver Award in the Intermediate Maths Challenge run by the UKMT and was selected, as part of a 4-person team to attend the UKMT Maths Olympiad at Pimlico Academy. I am on the Going for Gold Programme for elite sportswomen. ', 'special_interests' => 'I am a county level competitive swimmer.
I have an ARSM performance diploma on the piano.
