I have Grade 5 singing and will be performing in a local community opera in the summer.
I am currently doing the Duke of Edinburgh Silver Award, after completing the Bronze Award last summer.', 'special_skills' => 'Music, swimming and public speaking.', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I can play the piano, trombone and sing -  solo, or in an ensemble - and organise groups, having co-ordinated my house team for the school music competition last year. I can tell you about my experiences as a competitive swimmer.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I loved going on the National Children\'s Orchestra courses because I got to meet people from all around the UK. Now, I would like to expand my horizons even further by meeting people from around the world. I can learn new skills and enjoy activities I can\'t do in London, whilst learning about different cultures. I believe I can learn more from these Rotary camps than anything I can learn at school.', 'personal_remarks' => 'I enjoy meeting new people and trying new things and I am good at fitting in and working together in groups. So far I have only travelled abroad with family and school, but I am confident that I will adapt well to all the different people and activities on a Rotary camp.', 'place_of_birth' => 'London, UK', 'em_name' => 'Julie Rippon', 'em_relationship' => 'Aunt', 'em_htel' => '01737 778937', 'em_mobile' => '07917 876515', 'em_email' => 'julie_rippon@hotmail.co.uk', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3852.jpeg', 'date_of_app' => '2019-11-21 14:26:00'],
