ce I was thirteen. I also love swimming and maintaining fitness by going to the gym. ', 'attainment_vocation' => 'In year 11, I was very proud of my performance, especially in biology and chemistry. Seeing as I am interested in a medical career, this was very good news. In biology I averaged an 8 (8,8) and in chemistry I averaged a seven (7,8). I also got an A in maths and English. Overall, I was very proud of my GCSE grades and hope to carry on like this throughout my A-levels. ', 'special_interests' => 'I love science â€” I have chosen both biology and chemistry A levels which are both very challenging. I also have a passion for music, which I practice regularly, but I do not do it as a subject at sixth form. I play piano at a grade 8 level and am hoping to pass my grade 8 exam in the near future. I adore wildlife and nature, and have since a very young age â€” because of this, I have taken up the hobby of fish keeping as having my own little ecosystem in my bedroom is fascinating to me. ', 'special_skills' => 'I am a skilled performer as I have gained much experience over the years of performing musically . I am also quite skilled at boxing, which I picked up over the year I attended classes at Mikeyâ€™s boxing gym in Kidderminster. ', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'As mentioned, I play piano. I have performed countless times in the past with my friend, sometimes even getting payed for our performances! I hope to continue performing as it really helps me to have confidence in my ability and talent, which is something I often lack. ', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I enjoyed last yearâ€™s camp in Sicily, and would love another experience abroad. I hope to find a camp more associated with nature and wildlife, and to make yet more foreign friends. ', 'personal_remarks' => 'I am extremely personable, friendly, and easy to get along with. I love making friends and making others feel comfortable. I canâ€™t wait to meet a new group of friends next year when I go to my next camp. ',