            ['idapplication' => '975', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => false, 'dob' => '2002-09-11', 'gender' => true, 'email_address' => 'keelinbrennan@hotmail.co.uk', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'Presentation at School/College/University', 'firstname' => 'Keelin', 'surname' => 'Brennan', 'address' => '6 Corcrain Mews', 'city' => 'Portadown', 'county' => 'Armagh', 'postcode' => 'BT621HT', 'contact_no' => '+44 7843 797785', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7872 626519', 'parent_1' => 'Fiona McVeigh', 'parent_2' => 'Patrick Brennan', 'application_no' => '3882', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => 'Keelin', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1160', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Accepted', 'application_status_note' => '', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'fionamcveigh@hotmail.co.uk', 'parent2_email' => 'walterbrennan@sky.com', 'parent1_tel' => '', 'parent2_tel' => '', 'parent1_mobile' => '+44 7843 797785', 'parent2_mobile' => '+44 7889 816216', 'parent1_btel' => '', 'parent2_btel' => '', 'parent1_occupation' => 'Legal Secretary', 'parent2_occupation' => 'Heating Engineer', 'religion' => 'Roman Catholic ', 'diet_restriction' => 'None', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => false, 'drink_why' => '', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => true, 'treated_condition' => false, 'prescribed_meds' => false, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => 'Dormant asthma, I have not needed medication for over 2 years now.', 'rotary_club_id' => '19721', 'free_activities' => 'In my free time I attend Irish Dancing classes which I have been doing since I was four years old.  I also teach Irish Dancing classes to beginners who are three and four years old.  I like meeting up with friends at the weekend especially to go shopping or to the cinema.  I also spend time in the evenings on social media.  I love following fashion trends and keeping up with technology. I have a part time job in a phone shop as a retail advisor.  I really enjoy meeting new people and even though most of the staff are over twenty and all from different backgrounds I have a good relationship with them all.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I have been studying at St Patrick\'s Academy Dungannon since 2014.
At GCSE level I obtained grades;
A* English Language
A* Maths
A*A* Double Award Science
A* Digital Technology Programming
A Technology and Design
A Further Maths
A English Literature
A Irish
A Learning for Life and Work
A Religious Studies

I achieved the highest mark in my school year group in LLW and Digital Technology Programming.
I am currently studying Maths, Biology, Chemistry and Software Systems Development at AS Level.
I would like to study Human Biology at Queens University Belfast and then complete a PGCE course to become a secondary school Biology te', 'special_interests' => 'My special interest outside of school is Irish Dancing.  I have been doing it many years and couldn\'t imagine stopping. Over the years I have won many awards and have over 100 medals. I have made lots of friends through dancing and really enjoy it.  Every year my dancing school holds a dancing festival which I help to organise. I also volunteer at the local dancing festival each year as I love working with children. Inside of school my interest is Biology. I am very passionate about the subject and would love to teach it.  I completed my Irish GCSE in one year and received awards for achieving the highest mark in my year in two subjects.', 'special_skills' => 'I have taught the Irish language in a local primary school.
I teach Irish Dancing classes from beginner level right through to adults.
I have Irish Danced for a local rotary club luncheon.
I also Irish Dance at other private functions such as St Patrick\'s Day Events.
I am very organised which can be shown through my ability to arrange the sponsorship of awards for the dancing festival.
On the Ulster Project I developed leadership skills and have used them to teach young people. I also spoke to a lot of sponsors of the Ulster Project during my time in America and even did a presentation at one of the McPherson Rotary club\'s luncheon.', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I would be honoured to Irish Dance for the camp to traditional music and even pop music.
I would also love to teach the rest of the camp some Irish Dancing basics and even some conversational Irish.
', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I participated in the Ulster Project last July in which a group of teens from NI went to Kansas for a month.  This was an amazing experience and I made lifelong friends on the project.  I would love to participate in this experience as I love learning about different cultures from around the world and I think that this camp would be the perfect opportunity to do so.', 'personal_remarks' => 'I am very independent and I have gained a lot of confidence from the Ulster Project.  I hope to learn lots on this camp about different cultures and get an insight into people\'s experiences from around the world.  I am very mature and well-spoken as I even did a radio interview to promote the Ulster Project.
GO RAIBH MAITH AGAT !!!!
