pop/rock, folk, classical and worldwide music. I am interested in photography and enjoy taking photos. I go on long walks, such as through hills (Malvern Hills) or on local footpaths. I participate in water activities like canoeing and swimming and used to play badminton.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I have an A Level in French and three pending A Levels in English Language, German and History. I have received University offers to start a degree in European Studies in September 2020. ', 'special_interests' => 'I am passionate about learning languages and enjoy discovering cultures that are new to me. Having lived in France as a child, I developed a fascination with different festivals and traditions, as well as eating traditional dishes! Adapting to the "French way of life" through attending French school and getting involved with the local community has contributed to an open-minded attitude to life. ', 'special_skills' => 'I am bilingual in French. I can cook and prepare meals. ', 'contrib_entertainment' => '"One liner" jokes, charades.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I want to form friendships new people from different backgrounds. I enjoy learning about the world around me and I believe that the best way to do this is through travelling and meeting people. ', 'personal_remarks' => '', 'place_of_birth' => 'Birmingham, United Kingdom', 'em_name' => 'Alexander Simpson', 'em_relationship' => 'Brother', 'em_htel' => 'x', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7791 483411', 'em_email' => 'ajbsimpson@gmail.com', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3903.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-12-21 19:27:00'],
            ['idapplication' => '998', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => false, 'dob' => '2002-03-04', 'gender' => true, 'email_address' => 'Lindsay.brooke002@gmail.com', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'A Rotarian recommended it', 'firstname' => 'Brooke', 'surname' => 'Lindsay', 'address' => '14 st Margaret’s', 'city' => 'Quadring', 'county' => 'Lincolnshire', 'postcode' => 'Pe11 4pr', 'contact_no' => '+44 1775 822969', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7754 031002', 'parent_1' => 'Rebecca Jones', 'parent_2' => 'Christopher Jones', 'application_no' => '3904', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => '', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1070', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Withdrawn', 'application_status_note' => 'Paid Admin Fee', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'kwiatkowska.rebecca@gmail.com', 'parent2_email' => 'chris.jones@priory-cit.co.uk', 'parent1_tel' => '+44 1775 822969', 'parent2_tel' => '+44 1775 822969', 'parent1_mobile' => '+44 7804 124359', 'parent2_mobile' => '+44 7963 159801', 'parent1_btel' => '', 'parent2_btel' => '', 'parent1_occupation' => 'Foot Health Practitioner', 'parent2_occupation' => 'Premises manager', 'religion' => 'CofE', 'diet_restriction' => 'None ', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => false, 'drink_why' => '', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => false, 'treated_condition' => false, 'prescribed_meds' => true, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => 'Vitamin D Supplements', 'rotary_club_id' => '21457', 'free_activities' => 'In my free time I tend to revise for my teaching assistant apprenticeship college course, read and watch television. At the weekends I have also been apart of a young music leader programme of which I helped and supported young people and introduced to the arts, I also have been completing the bronze arts award through this. I am also very interested in art and work on individual projects. I try to travel as much as I can and have recently reurned from volunteering at a summer camp in bulgaria teaching young children english.
', 'attainment_vocation' => 'After I complete my Apprenticeship as a teaching assistant. I plan to further my studies at university carrying on the route of teaching. To help me with this I have partook in many organisations of which i have gained valuable work experience in teaching and child care fields, as well as this I have taken part in schemes to further my experience such as a language leader award of which I delivered the basics of German to young people. To gain more experience in other areas such as independence and to experience more culture would help me greatly achieve my goals in pursuing a teaching career.', 'special_interests' => 'I thoroughly enjoyed and was heavily involved in the Air Training Corps, whilst being there I achieved the rank of cadet corporal within my first year of being there, I received awards for Officers Commanding choice and top shot of the year, I was also first aid trained and became comfortable in a leadership role as a corporal and through controlling media platforms associated with the Corps. I have also been a part of many programs at school such the Bronze Duke of Edinburgh Award and the bronze arts award.', 'special_skills' => 'Through all of my extra curricular programs I have been apart of and working with children I have learnt to be resilient, patient and a good team player. I work well with people and I am confident in meeting new people.
', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'Sadly I cannot contribute to entertainment musically or in a comedic sense and don\'t perform well, I am much better suited to the organising aspect and in past experiences prefer to be backstage.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'My reason for Participation is that this is an incredible once in a lifetime opportunity that I would love to be a part of. I am fascinated with religion and culture. I would love to experience it first hand. I think it would also be beneficial with my chosen career path and would get a wider understanding of various cultures and religions. It would also give me an amazing insight to different parts of the world which would otherwise be difficult to obtain and learn from.
', 'personal_remarks' => 'I love meeting new people and would love to make connections and relationships with different people from around the globe.
', 'place_of_birth' => 'Peterborough, England ', 'em_name' => 'Paul Kwiatkowski', 'em_relationship' => 'Grandfather', 'em_htel' => '+44 1775 248734', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7780 377191', 'em_email' => 'pfklincsuk@gmail.com', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3904.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-12-22 10:48:00'],
            ['idapplication' => '999', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => false, 'dob' => '2002-04-30', 'gender' => false, 'email_address' => '60garvey@gmail.com', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'Presentation at School/College/University', 'firstname' => 'Peter', 'surname' => 'McClements', 'address' => '60 Favour Royal Road', 'city' => 'Aughnacloy', 'county' => 'Co Tyrone', 'postcode' => 'BT696BR', 'contact_no' => '+44 28 8555 7260', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7379 429123', 'parent_1' => 'Fiona McClements', 'parent_2' => 'Derek McClements', 'application_no' => '3907', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => 'Peter', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1160', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Accepted', 'application_status_note' => '', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'fiona.mcclements@btopenworld.com', 'parent2_email' => '', 'parent1_tel' => '+44 28 8555 7260', 'parent2_tel' => '+44 28 8555 7260', 'parent1_mobile' => '+44 7565 099304', 'parent2_mobile' => '', 'parent1_btel' => '+44 7748 148703', 'parent2_btel' => '', 'parent1_occupation' => 'Enviromental Health Worker', 'parent2_occupation' => 'Farmer', 'religion' => 'Christian', 'diet_restriction' => 'None', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => false, 'drink_why' => '', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => false, 'treated_condition' => false, 'prescribed_meds' => false, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => '', 'rotary_club_id' => '19721', 'free_activities' => 'I live on a farm so there is always work to do, looking after animals after school and driving tractors in the summer. I also have a part time job in a butcherâ€™s shop. I have enjoyed being a scout for 13 years and have been a volunteer leader for the younger organisations for the past 3 years. I have fun outdoors with camping, canoeing, fire building and cooking. I play and watch all sorts of sports. I have played rugby for 7 years and love not only the game but being part of a team. I also enjoy playing snooker and golf and cricket. I love going out with my friends at the weekends and love to watch movies and listening to music. ', 'attainment_vocation' => 'In school I have attained 4 A*s, 3Aâ€™s and 2Bâ€™s at my GCSEâ€™s, in my ASâ€™s I have 4A grades and am currently studying Chemistry, physics and maths at A level. In my school I was made prefect and was finance manager in the young enterprise initiative but was also a member of the schools Research and development team. I had a major role in the school play and in sport I am cricket captain, and a member of the 1st XV rugby squad. I really enjoy meeting new people, being part of a team, and challenging myself which are some of the reasons why I want to study medicine at university next year. If all goes to plan, I want to be a surgeon in the', 'special_interests' => 'I have a special interest in meeting people and being part of a team. I loved being selected for World Scout Jamboree in America where I experienced different cultures and met people from countless countries. I was also the sole NI representative on the UKC Impact team which helped to plan, consult and co-ordinate events at the jamboree for the participating scouts. I have attained my bronze Duke of Edinburgh award and have started my silver. I have a special interest in watching and playing all sports but especially rugby. I was cricket player of the year last year due to my bowling skill and won Junior Prize day at my local golf club. ', 'special_skills' => 'I have good communication skills which I have developed from my genuine interest in people.  As captain of the cricket team I developed my teamwork and motivational skills to try and keep all the players motivated to play their best. I am a good listener which was useful at Scout jamboree when there were some tensions due to the close living area and scouts wanted to talk to some-one. I am a good public speaker as had a major part in my school Play.  I have good manual dexterity skills which are essential for the level of butchery tasks I carry out. I have passed my driving test and enjoy driving both cars and tractors. ', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'Although I canâ€™t read music, I have taught myself to play the piano at home over the last few months and hopefully will keep developing my skills. I am happy to take part in speaking roles and playing music and I would also be able to organise different types of entertainment. As part of the UK Impact team I have experience of planning activities for groups and encouraging everyone to get involved. I have experience as a scout leader for younger children also. I would be able to tell a few jokes in front of a group due to my experience in school plays but nothing too funny I have to warn you.', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I applied for the Rotary scheme as I had a presentation in my school, and it seemed like an amazing opportunity to try and develop myself as a person. I want to increase my knowledge of the world through experiencing different cultures, visiting new places and meeting new people. I am comfortable in new situations and making the first move to talk to others.  Being a part of a camp would help me understand new cultures and further develop my social and personal skills which are so instrumental in my future career of medicine. I want to make new friends, be part of an international team and have some fun.  ', 'personal_remarks' => '', 'place_of_birth' => 'Craigavon, Co. Armagh, Northern Ireland', 'em_name' => 'Linda Mcclelland', 'em_relationship' => 'Aunt', 'em_htel' => '+44 28 8556 8077', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7733 445778', 'em_email' => 'lindaandjim16@gmail.com', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3907.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-12-22 16:24:00'],
            ['idapplication' => '1000', 'emergency_contact' => false, 'parent_div_sep' => false, 'dob' => '2002-07-23', 'gender' => false, 'email_address' => 'amcb2002@googlemail.com', 'school' => null, 'why_rotary' => null, 'consider_alt_country' => null, 'how_did_you_hear' => 'Presentation at School/College/University', 'firstname' => 'Adam', 'surname' => 'McBride', 'address' => '15 St Andrews Way', 'city' => 'Bromsgrove', 'county' => 'Worcestershire', 'postcode' => 'B617NR', 'contact_no' => '+44 1527 570477', 'alt_contact_no' => '+44 7443 626768', 'parent_1' => 'Julie Dawn Marie McBride', 'parent_2' => 'George Neil McBride', 'application_no' => '3908', 'citizen_of' => 'UK', 'other_info' => null, 'exchange_type' => 'CAMPS & TOURS', 'pref_name' => 'Adam', 'parent_support' => false, 'dyeo_id' => '1060', 'realm' => 'USER', 'application_status' => 'Accepted', 'application_status_note' => 'Paid Admin Fee', 'dyeo_assigned' => true, 'application_fee' => null, 'application_fee_paid' => false, 'parent1_rotarian' => false, 'parent2_rotarian' => false, 'parent1_rotary_club' => '', 'parent2_rotary_club' => '', 'parent1_email' => 'jdmm52@googlemail.com', 'parent2_email' => 'gnmcb1@gmail.com', 'parent1_tel' => '+44 1527 570477', 'parent2_tel' => '+44 1527 570477', 'parent1_mobile' => '+44 7703 781158', 'parent2_mobile' => '+44 7702 107477', 'parent1_btel' => '', 'parent2_btel' => '', 'parent1_occupation' => 'Tutor', 'parent2_occupation' => 'Programme Manager', 'religion' => 'None', 'diet_restriction' => 'None', 'smoke' => false, 'smoke_why' => '', 'drink' => false, 'drink_why' => '', 'illegal_drugs' => false, 'illegal_drugs_why' => '', 'native_language' => 'English', 'medical_condition' => false, 'treated_condition' => false, 'prescribed_meds' => false, 'special_req' => false, 'medical_info' => '', 'rotary_club_id' => '19064', 'free_activities' => 'Swimming, cycling, playing golf, reading fiction books, programming applications, playing video games, watching movies and tv, solving the Rubik\'s cube, making electronics projects and circuits.', 'attainment_vocation' => 'I am studying computer science, physics, maths and further maths at A Level, and I hope to be studying Computer Systems Engineering at University in the near future as that is where my interests lie. I have participated in several maths related competitions (such as the UKMT), scoring highly in most of them. I have also taken part in some physics competitions (such as the Physics Olympiad), which I have scored reasonably highly in. I have attained really good grades at GCSE and hope to do so with my A levels.', 'special_interests' => 'I\'m especially interested in the interaction between software and hardware more than anything else, as I find it fascinating how code can make hardware do things physically. I have managed to get onto several extra curricular courses relating to physics and computer science after a thorough application process. These have allowed me to expand my knowledge of these fields and gave me experience with talking to lecturers and asking questions that will get the information I am looking for. I have also completed bronze and silver D of E Award, which has been a big accomplishment for me, and I am part way through completing my gold D of E.', 'special_skills' => 'I do lighting for my school\'s performances and manage the technical team that take part in those performances. This has allowed me to learn new things quickly, as well as practise troubleshooting and fixing things quickly if it affects a performance. I can also build circuits and program applications, which has been useful for working on my own projects. I am also able to deal with multiple large things happening at once without getting stressed, which I consider to be a useful skill, as I do many things outside of academia.', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I could present maths problems and puzzles to other people, which I find enjoyable. I can also have a good conversation about anything that me and another person have in common in terms of interests. I believe I could also teach people how to solve the Rubix\'s cube, which would be a fun night in my opinion. ', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I want to take part in this program because I would like the chance of experiencing an activity that I haven\'t done / have done little of before in a completely different environment to the one I\'m used to. I would also like to develop social skills for getting on with people I have never met before as that is a skill that I think would be really useful to have. I would very much like the chance of being immersed in another language as well, as I haven\'t been able to learn a language properly from what I\'ve been taught in school.', 'personal_remarks' => 'I also have some experience with sailing and kayaking through courses I\'ve done previously at the local activity centre, both of which I enjoy immensely. I also have some experience climbing with the climbing walls at various activity centres.', 'place_of_birth' => 'Redditch, UK', 'em_name' => 'Edith McBride', 'em_relationship' => 'Grandparent', 'em_htel' => '+44 28 6865 8466', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7845 478714', 'em_email' => 'gemcb@hotmail.co.uk', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3908.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-12-24 11:01:00'],
