requent the local youth club every week. I have womenâ€™s group at the youth club after choir practice in school and I also stay after school for the Pope John Paul II Award.  I play soccer once in a while and I have Young Enterprise and Halo group every Wednesday but I have to alternate between them as theyâ€™re on at the same time. Last December, we had to showcase our companyâ€™s product (Mental Health Awareness bracelets) which was a thrilling experience and I also had the chance to experience something new by food packing with other people for Halo group. Furthermore, I volunteer for the juniors at the youth club every Friday which I ', 'attainment_vocation' => ' I am a member of the Mental Health and Wellbeing team in school and we meet every Wednesday at lunchtime. Also I am currently taking part in the Young Enterprise programme and we meet frequently to create our product. I was a representative for the Anti-bullying team for three years. I achieved the highest mark in the school for Spanish and Child Development in my year and I Won the Contribution to the Arts Award in my school for two consecutive years', 'special_interests' => 'I volunteer at the local youth club on a weekly basis, assisting the staff by looking after the juniors and working the cash register. I have a great passion for music and I enjoy learning different instruments. Iâ€™ve recently been wanting to learn the cello lately as well as tennis but I just canâ€™t find the time in my schedule to do them. Iâ€™m Iâ€™m also very interested in travelling as well and Iâ€™ve recently returned from a trip to Rome after on a school trip to Salamanca last year.
', 'special_skills' => 'I would say that Iâ€™m very well at adapting to new environment and an example would be the fact that I moved over to Ireland when I was  quite young and I had learn a whole new culture and language - which was very challenging at first but I very quickly learned. Iâ€™ve also got excellent communication and leadership skills which Iâ€™ve acquired by joining different clubs i.e the girlâ€™s rugby club, youth club and Gaelic etc. Iâ€™m also very committed  and I dedicate myself to activities which Iâ€™m very passionate about. ', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'Yes and Iâ€™ve actually received the schoolâ€™s  â€˜Contribution to the Artsâ€™ award at Prize giving for two consecutive years. Iâ€™ve played the tin whistle since I was 8 and Iâ€™ve also been a member of the school choir throughout primary and secondary school. Iâ€™m always required to participate in every event, for example, Iâ€™m always singing and playing at school prize givings, school mass, open nights and also during Christmas when the choir goes carolling. ', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I have always wanted join a camp abroad and as soon as I was informed about this programme, I immediately signed up. I thought that it was a great opportunity for me (and other young people) to develop our cultural knowledge and be more open minded about trying out new things. I feel that this programme will enhance my self-confidence, simply because I would have the chance to meet new people and I would be required to step out of my comfort zone. I think that it provides a great opportunity for young people to socialise as well as experience new things. ', 'personal_remarks' => 'The Rotary Exchange programme would motivate me to step out of my comfort zone and allow me the chance to experience a whole new culture and appreciate the diversity thatâ€™s in this world. ', 'place_of_birth' => 'Dungannon, Co. Tyrone, Northern Ireland', 'em_name' => 'Francisco Sousa', 'em_relationship' => 'Uncle', 'em_htel' => '', 'em_mobile' => '+44 7884 829088', 'em_email' => '', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3910.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-12-25 21:33:00'],
