oyal School Dungannon from Year 8. I am also a member of Dungannon Swimmimg club and I represent Dungannon Boys\' Brigade at several sporting activities including cross country, netball and football. To ensure a high level of fitness, I regularly attend the gym and I enjoy attending Youth club activities as a means of relaxation and an opportunity to have fund with my friends. I also volunteer in the junior section of Boys\' Brigade and in a Husky dog centre and more recently in Loane House, South Tyrone hospital. ', 'attainment_vocation' => 'A2 level: Maths pending, Chemistry pending, Physics pending
As level: Maths A, Physics A, Design and Technology A, Chemitsry B
GCSE: Maths A*, Further Maths A*, Physics A*, Design and Technology A*, Chemisry A, Biology A, English language A, English literature A,French A, Music A.', 'special_interests' => 'In sixth form at RSD, I am a Prefect, House Secretary and a committed member of the Charities Committee. In Year 13, I was also involved in the Sentinus Research and Development scheme, resulting in me achieving a Gold crest award. I also received my Silver Duke of Edinburgh in Year 13 and I am presently working towards my Gold. I have also just completed my Queen\'s Badge for BB, having achieved my President\'s badge last year.  I had worthwhile work experience in the Cardiothoracic ward of the Royal Victoria hospital, work shadowing consultants and junior doctors do their rounds and getting the opportunity to see heart surgery in action. ', 'special_skills' => 'I am a highly enthusiastic, hard-working individual who gives of his best in everything that he does. My experiences both inside and outside of school have developed my communication, organisational, leadership and problem-solving skills, my ability to work well as part of a team and my capapcity to think on my feet, showcasing my determination to succeed, my powers of resilience and perseverance and my overall energy, commitment and dedication. I am also a caring and compassionate person who gets on extremely well with others, who has proven himself to be highly responsibile and relaible and who would not give up in the face of challenge. ', 'contrib_entertainment' => 'I have my Grade 6 in piano and I also play the piano accordion. ', 'reason_for_camp' => 'I would foresee both personal and professional benefits. Working alongside a diverse group of peers from a variety of nationalities would make me more accepting and respectful of others in general. Working with such a team would also develop my skills of communication, emotional empathy, and decision-making all of which are relevant for a future career in medicine. The emphasis on the outdoors would also be appealing, allowing me to pursue my love of sports  and the opportunity to spend time in a different country without my familiy, would devlop my skills of independence and confidence, preparing me for future life in university. ', 'personal_remarks' => 'Engaging in such a programme has also been a keen aspiration of mine, and listening to feedback from others who had the privilege of taking part in this programme before has really spurred me on to be part of such an adventure. ', 'place_of_birth' => 'Belfast, Northern Ireland, UK', 'em_name' => 'Pearl Clarke', 'em_relationship' => 'Grandmother', 'em_htel' => '+44 28 8772 5563', 'em_mobile' => '', 'em_email' => '', 'country_citizenship' => null, 'image_location' => 'uploads/pict_app3915.png', 'date_of_app' => '2019-12-30 11:12:00'],
